{"event_type":"review","id":"47a23aa46077c53838559185e4ac0b06777da748c86e8ea7b2ad5d1607eccaff","occurred_at":"2026-11-13T20:22:32Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/32f10ec08e72d1fdb84a11139b9614fb417a63bea6065ad09c179bfe765b6271","sha256":"32f10ec08e72d1fdb84a11139b9614fb417a63bea6065ad09c179bfe765b6271"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2bb3794d5f89a6e82f9d49e232aeaa185a0847db31c31bb1c52f0d38b5279411","sha256":"2bb3794d5f89a6e82f9d49e232aeaa185a0847db31c31bb1c52f0d38b5279411"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9e8e8c360583fb41589d6342da4ed4c5a987c8a3f8f6fcad155fa6dfc7554da4","sha256":"9e8e8c360583fb41589d6342da4ed4c5a987c8a3f8f6fcad155fa6dfc7554da4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6e00ca048480a5eeb41bf827889d725e0818498ffbbe16ae5c0332acb7d4303b","sha256":"6e00ca048480a5eeb41bf827889d725e0818498ffbbe16ae5c0332acb7d4303b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9c7181128917e6ab7071bf1419a9c384b3f6bd9a1dd933f422c6ac62c3dd5bf1","sha256":"9c7181128917e6ab7071bf1419a9c384b3f6bd9a1dd933f422c6ac62c3dd5bf1"}],"attempt_id":"de90fbe4aa7cdb9f779337aee125b6bb3f1287aff3327c7d7657a22fb051a08b:0:1","base":"90e8375c61d03098bdd6820299c4f9b3b182e7d9","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"5f8396e6bd23a88f37f19bf05fcc3b27dd366bc2","body":"**Preserve canonical newline bytes when writing vectors.**\n\nAt `apps/crq-python/pr_review_findings_vector_emit_b1.py:947`, `write_text` uses platform newline translation. On Windows, regeneration therefore writes CRLF instead of LF, contrary to the byte-identical guarantee. The `read_text` comparison on Line 950 normalizes those newlines and does not detect the difference. Python 3.14 documents both behaviors. ([docs.python.org](https://docs.python.org/3.14/library/pathlib.html))\n\nWrite and compare UTF-8 bytes. Apply the same canonical-byte policy to `--stdout` on Line 943.","id":"5949d462637a36e8dbeae7f9f57050e8c85df1b62dd7ca50067810fddc4edf9c","intervals":[[947,947]],"path":"apps/crq-python/pr_review_findings_vector_emit_b1.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Preserve canonical newline bytes when writing vectors."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"5f8396e6bd23a88f37f19bf05fcc3b27dd366bc2","body":"**Model per-page `gh --jq` evaluation in the vector emitter.**\n\n`_apply_reviews_jq` treats the paginated reviews response as one jq input stream. `gh api --paginate --jq` evaluates the filter once for each page response. The `<stdin>:N` error locations derived from the concatenated stream do not match that behavior. The `reviews-page-*-row-error` expectations record these locations and may not match the page-local locations the command reports.\n\nEvaluate the selector separately for each page in the fake. Record page-local error locations, then regenerate the affected expectations.","id":"6b4ce36aeb1b1324990e9c4c64855dac94bb0289da3c0ed49f82a0c540524f97","intervals":[[267,272]],"path":"apps/crq-python/pr_review_findings_vector_emit_b1.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Model per-page `gh --jq` evaluation in the vector emitter."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"1fc08c284e08427640a7c49f895d036fb556678f","body":"**Preserve `receipt-unavailable` for subsequent status and retries.**\n\nIf the latest completed candidate has an unavailable receipt, admission returns `next_action=\"resubmit\"` and `reason=\"receipt-unavailable\"`. These fields exist only in the response.\n\nA subsequent `status()` or identical submission calls `status()` again. Because `adequate()` checks only the stored receipt ID, that response reports completion without the recovery instruction, although the receipt remains unavailable.\n\nPersist this condition or revalidate the receipt when producing status and retry responses.","id":"b15a31b32760941fdea4c6bbfa73ea0c59f5bfadc7b5cc9be32c3f98e2626f6e","intervals":[[112,113]],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_admission.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Preserve `receipt-unavailable` for subsequent status and retries."}],"head":"2ddb94640a2006fefed707d558cf37be52cd0ce2","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"f84c5b69535a5bc412da3e94c4446edbb3017a49","intervals":[[1,820]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ledger_vector_emit_b1.py"},{"blob":"5f8396e6bd23a88f37f19bf05fcc3b27dd366bc2","intervals":[[1,960]],"path":"apps/crq-python/pr_review_findings_vector_emit_b1.py"},{"blob":"1bd2d1a9782e506956985a0b9921b609f388dcf2","intervals":[[1,1287]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_prepare_vectors.py"},{"blob":"1fc08c284e08427640a7c49f895d036fb556678f","intervals":[[1,128]],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_admission.py"},{"blob":"9885ea3149110dc2a4d7ec9b793c4a5dfc0c9b0f","intervals":[[1,115]],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_notify.py"},{"blob":"5e964168cc896f7165f1b980012965e992761ab2","intervals":[[1,179]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_fixtures.py"},{"blob":"f48e3dbcad41171ec758f2feb50ba5afacfd312f","intervals":[[1,335]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_rollback_plan.py"},{"blob":"797e21fe5fbebfbfba8b48e19fd48c87a097b8a8","intervals":[[1,171]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_review_notify.py"}],"job_id":"de90fbe4aa7cdb9f779337aee125b6bb3f1287aff3327c7d7657a22fb051a08b:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"f84c5b69535a5bc412da3e94c4446edbb3017a49","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/ledger_vector_emit_b1.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"5f8396e6bd23a88f37f19bf05fcc3b27dd366bc2","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"app